  "question": {
    "text": "Two rigid boxes containing different ideal gases are placed on a table. Box A contains one mole of nitrogen at temperature $T_0$, while Box $B$ contains one mole of helium at temperature $(7 / 3) T_0$. The boxes are then put into thermal contact with each other and heat flows between them until the gases reach a common final temperature. (Ignore the heat capacity of boxes). Then, the final temperature of the gases, $T_f$, in terms of $T_0$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "CDI5n",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{f}}=\\frac{5}{2} \\mathrm{~T}_0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "O2BSL",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{f}}=\\frac{3}{7} \\mathrm{~T}_0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DWdyi",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{f}}=\\frac{7}{3} \\mathrm{~T}_0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "QL6CP",
      "text": "\n$T_f=\\frac{3}{2} T_0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\Delta \\mathrm{U}=0$\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{3}{2} \\mathrm{R}\\left(\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{f}}-\\mathrm{T}_0\\right)+1 \\times \\frac{5}{2} \\mathrm{R}\\left(\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{f}}-\\frac{7}{3} \\mathrm{~T}_0\\right)=0$\n$\\mathrm{~T}_{\\mathrm{f}}=\\frac{3}{2} \\mathrm{~T}_0$",
    "image": null
  },
